{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Second audit pass (2026-10-26, worktree at `b6e723ceb59` + the landing `d279` change). Two things beyond the line-number drift already recorded.\n\n**1. `d279` introduces a test that this story will break.**\n\n`d279` adds `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots`, whose assertion is literally:\n\n```python\nassert [line.split(\":\")[0] for line in hits] == [\"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py\"]\n```\n\nIt greps `src/rebar/llm/evals` for `docs/experiments` and requires `corpus.py` to be the **sole** remaining match (that is `d279`'s AC1). This story's Approach repoints `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:5` to the new path — at which point the grep returns an EMPTY list and that assertion fails. The two stories are individually correct and jointly red.\n\nResolution belongs to this story, since it is the one that moves the tree: when `corpus.py`'s docstring is repointed, `test_no_hard_coded_roots` must be updated in the same change — either to expect no matches at all, or repointed at `evals`. Add `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py` to `file_impact` and name the update in the Approach.\n\n**2. `file_impact` is missing 6 files that the story's own grep AC will catch.**\n\nAC2 requires the repo-wide grep to print nothing outside frozen fixtures and historical notes. These currently match and are **not** in `file_impact`:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` — the `[llm.evals]` section comment `d279` adds names `docs/experiments`\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py` — see item 1 (new in `d279`)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_cli_paths.py` — module docstring (new in `d279`)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` — note `d279`'s AC asserts this file is *unchanged*; that holds only until this story moves the tree\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_interpreter_v2.py`\n- `.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-failure-disposition-contract.eval.yaml`\n\nAlso `.test_durations` matches, but it is generated and should be left alone — worth stating explicitly so the grep AC does not read as requiring an edit there.\n\n**Line-number corrections for the remaining test cites** (first match per file, on `b6e723ceb59`), in addition to those in the previous comment:\n\n| Description cite | Actual |\n|---|---|\n| `test_decomp_shape_criterion.py:183` | `:179` |\n| `test_necessity_criterion.py:103` | `:98` |\n| `test_project_failure_disposition_contract.py:242` | `:222` |\n| `test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py:163-170` | `:148,149` |\n| `test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:168,212` | `:169,210` |\n| `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py:12` | **no match at all** — the reference is gone; drop it from Scope and `file_impact` |\n\nRe-verified as accurate: `test_ac_process_gate_criterion.py:118`, `test_asserted_capability_criterion.py:115`, `test_t15_overlay_derisk_criterion.py:156`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:25`, `tests/unit/test_check_dco_identity.py:6,110`, `tests/scripts/test_classify_gerrit_verify_change.py:57-58`.\n\nWhole-tree count for sizing: 54 files currently match outside `docs/experiments/`, `docs/calibration/`, `tests/fixtures/`, `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md`. The `docs/adr/` (4), `docs/research/` (1) and `docs/archive/` (1) hits are historical records and are correctly excluded by AC2's \"historical notes\" carve-out — worth naming them in Scope as deliberately untouched so a reviewer does not read the grep as requiring them."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793083797337788655,"uuid":"4f0d9539-fc2d-4e43-a6e8-1bf1ea247559"}